  "prefLabel": "Bea 502.12 Cottage courts",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Bea 502.12 “Cottage courts” means a type of missing middle housing that are a grouping of small, detached structures clustered around a shared common area, and developed with a plan for the entire site, including having the unit entrances facing the shared common area.\n\nSource. #14043, eff 8-8-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/bea500.html"
